WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Ever thought about how insane submarines are? No?&nbsp;
Well, I do. I think about this all the time. I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.300
not talking about these cute little science&nbsp;
explorers. I'm talking about these massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.000
military nuclear attack submarines, these&nbsp;
windowless spaceships of the ocean strapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.640
with ballistic missiles that have nuclear warheads&nbsp;
on them. These things travel underwater in stealth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.500
mode through complete darkness for months at a&nbsp;
time. They move slowly to avoid making noise so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.540
they won't be detected by enemies. They're&nbsp;
even coated with rubbery tile that absorbs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.500
sound so that sonar can’t bounce up against&nbsp;
them. So the question I always have is like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.580
don't they run into things like whales or&nbsp;
something? It turns out they don't. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.480
most of the time they don't. They put out&nbsp;
sound into the ocean and whatever it bounces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.220
off gives them a map of what is ahead of them.&nbsp;
But also, maps! Look at these beautiful maps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.960
of the ocean floor. But sometimes they're&nbsp;
wrong. In 2005, this submarine ran into an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.860
underground mountain because of an error&nbsp;
in one of their maps. Well, regardless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.820
I would rather take my chance out there on the&nbsp;
ocean. Submarines are really freakin’ cool.

